<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Offers the SL_SanguophageLair mutator on Odyssey landmarks, the way the Stockpile mutator
    is offered (0.05 on most landmarks, 0.15 on the man-made and dune ones, 0.25 on frozen
    ruins). Odyssey-only: lives in the compat root so the xpath can't miss without the DLC
    (a PatchOperationAdd whose xpath matches nothing logs an error).

    Each landmark rolls its mutatorChances independently at world generation
    (WorldLandmarks.AddLandmark), so the chance is per landmark of that kind, not per world.
    A default planet carries roughly TilesCount * 0.0022 landmarks (WorldGenStep_Landmarks),
    weighted by LandmarkDef.commonality, which is what makes the numbers below land at "a few
    lairs per world": enough to be found while the mapgen is being iterated on, rare enough to
    stay a discovery. Tuning knob for later: a settings slider writing MutatorChance.chance.

    Landmark picks: the rock-and-hollow landmarks (a lair is cut into stone, and a cliff or
    chasm is where an ancient stairwell reads as native) at the higher chance; the ancient
    man-made landmarks at the lower one, as a lair reusing older ruins. Wet, lava, coastal and
    ice landmarks are left out: nothing to carve, or nowhere sanguophages would settle.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/LandmarkDef[defName="Cavern" or defName="Chasm" or defName="Crevasse" or defName="Hollow" or defName="Cliffs" or defName="Plateau" or defName="Valley" or defName="Basin"]/mutatorChances</xpath>
    <value>
      <SL_SanguophageLair>0.15</SL_SanguophageLair>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/LandmarkDef[defName="Ruins" or defName="FrozenRuins" or defName="AncientQuarry"]/mutatorChances</xpath>
    <value>
      <SL_SanguophageLair>0.05</SL_SanguophageLair>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
